Pet arch-lichs are pretty dangerous if you don't have MR. In my
current game, I've got a 15th level Valkyrie with a pet arch-lich, and
it's already cost me my only "oLS because I don't have a source of MR
yet. It got confused and did the old touch of death to me. I tried
dropping a unicorn horn and a potion of full healing, but it wouldn't
use either. Having a confused pet arch-lich following you around via
teleport when you know it's one more touch of death from ending your
game is not fun. It eventually got better, but I'm really wishing I
had a source of MR. That'll be my first wish.

Plus there's the issue of it killing every temple priest, shopkeeper,
nurse and foocubi that you really want to be able to interact with.
You can't just lock it in a isolated room because it teleports back to
you. You really don't want to leave it on another level while you
transact your business, because it will become less tame. And since it
doesn't eat, you have no way to increase its tameness, so sooner or
later you'll come back and find it's not your pet anymore. Then you've
got to deal with a pretty nasty monster with a lot of HP and that
touch of death thing. But at least it respects Elbereth - when it's
not confused, that is.

I'm pretty hesitant to head down to the castle because i expect I'll
run into at least one purple L there and I don't want to do that
without MR. I've got a genocide scroll, so I would normally bless it
and genocide Ls, but that would kill my pet as well. At least there
isn't a penalty for genociding your own pet, so I'm pretty tempted to
do it.

